"""Element Test Lab - cubes, beams, slabs and columns, one result per sensor channel, checked against IS-code limits.

HONESTY NOTES
* The limits below are the team's reading of the Indian Standards (IS 456:2000, IS 516, IS 13311). They were NOT
  checked against the purchased BIS text (several were cross-checked only against secondary web summaries). Every rule
  carries `verify=True` and is shown in the app with that flag. Use this as a lab-bench helper, never as a certificate.
* Simulated tests are generated by simple physical formulas plus noise (see `simulate`). Manual tests use the numbers
  the engineer types in. Both go through the SAME evaluator.
* RF-coil readings have no code basis (experimental sensor); they are INFO only.
* Each sensor channel is independent: a channel with no data is INACTIVE and simply left out of the element index.
"""
